From 996e61a15d2755e44727e971ecdb005fcc1c6374 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PromethenDev <PromethenDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 09:38:39 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 133/149] kernel: keep guest file handles when their content
 root closes (card S5-2 endless loading)

ContentManager::CloseOpenedFilesFromContent released the guest's still-open XFile handles when the
game closed a content root (it closes its DLC roots while Wwise still streams sound\*.pck). The
freed numbers were reused at once, so the guest's own later NtClose hit the next owner (Bink's
mutex), and the number was then reused by DLC_01.pck: Bink waited on a file forever (black
loading screen, GitHub #29/#72/#83/#84). New cvar WWE2K14_CONTENT_CLOSE_KEEP_FILES (default on)
keeps the handles; every case is logged as [content-close].

Diagnostics: freeze report lists each blocked thread's guest call chain and, for file waits, the
path and the slot's previous owner + closer; [stale-handle] warns on waits on closed handles;
optional WWE2K14_HANDLE_ROUND_ROBIN handle allocation (default off).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
